 "name": "Maximum: Instrumentalization",
 "type": "feat",
 "img": "modules/jjk5e/icons/techniques/regalia.svg",
 "system": {
  "description": {
   "value": "<p><em>Prerequisite: Must have Soul Bound Treasure</em></p>\n<p>You have learned to apply your soul control to a wide area, turning everything within your sight into a Lesser Regalia that obeys your will. As an action for 8 CE, you turn nonmagical objects around you that are not being worn or carried into Lesser Regalia that destroy what lies before you. This creates a 60 ft cone originating from you. Any creatures within range must make a Dexterity saving throw, taking 10d10 necrotic damage and be pushed back 30 feet and knocked prone on a failed save or half as much and not pushed back or prone on a successful save. A creature that is pushed back and impacts a solid object or structure takes 3d6 bludgeoning damage. Objects and structures in range take maximum damage. A creature that fails their save against this technique has their maximum hit points reduced by the damage taken until they finish a long rest. If the creature failed their save, this damage cannot be reduced.</p>",
   "chat": ""
  },
